# Cost, agents, and models (global hard rule)

## Models

- Prefer the cheapest capable model/path first.
- Main chat model is user-controlled (Composer); do not fight settings.
- When spawning agents or choosing models, follow cheap-and-capable-first.
- Escalate only with a short justification.

## Agents

- Default: **1** implementation agent.
- Hard maximum without further user approval after the fact report: **5**.
- If using more than 1 agent, report: count, reason, expected benefit.
- If approaching or using 5, report clearly why 5 were needed (usage review).

## Context

- Do not forward the full user prompt to every specialist.
- Each specialist gets only relevant requirements, files, and decisions.
- Prefer references to existing summaries over duplicating large context.
- Do not spawn agents or invoke skills because they exist — only when required.

## Skills

- Orchestrate existing skills; do not recreate their functionality.
- Skip planning/brainstorming/browser research on trivial work.
- Browser automation via MCP when automating the browser; browser QC via skill when validating UI quality.
